WEBVTT

00:04:28.916 --> 00:04:31.196
that's frequently used by coaches,

00:04:31.196 --> 00:04:33.196
players, commentators, experts.

00:04:33.236 --> 00:04:34.796
It goes like this:

00:04:34.796 --> 00:04:36.916
the league table never lies.

00:04:37.596 --> 00:04:42.436
It kind of assumes that once the last game
of a season is played,

00:04:42.476 --> 00:04:44.156
justice prevails.

00:04:44.196 --> 00:04:47.636
The team that finishes top of the table
is the best-performing team,

00:04:47.676 --> 00:04:50.556
and the teams that relegate
are the worst-performing teams.

00:04:50.596 --> 00:04:53.716
At the end of the day,
everyone gets what they deserve.

00:04:54.196 --> 00:04:56.036
It's not that simple, actually.

00:04:56.076 --> 00:04:57.916
And let me explain why.

00:04:57.916 --> 00:05:00.196
Please meet Matthew Benham.